#!/usr/bin/env -S bashy --bashsharp
~~~skill as guide
---
name: google
description: Google Workspace CLI wrapper for Gmail, Calendar, Tasks, Drive, and self-service BYOP onboarding.
metadata:
  requires: "has=bashy"
---
# Google Workspace CLI (google.bsh)

Agent-friendly Bash# wrapper around the Tier-6 managed external gws (googleworkspace/cli).
Provides self-service Bring-Your-Own-Project (BYOP) onboarding, explicit per-account credential
isolation, secret-in-argv refusal, 25 MiB Drive upload preflight, and composable multi-service
workflows across Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Tasks, and Google Drive.

## Self-Service BYOP Onboarding (Free $0 Google Cloud Project per User)

Because Gmail and Drive use Google Restricted Scopes (which cap unverified shared OAuth clients
at 100 users and share project-level quotas), each user or tenant provisions their own $0 Google
Cloud project:

  bashy google auth-guide account=alice@example.com project=my-bashy-gws
  bashy google auth-setup account=alice@example.com project=my-bashy-gws
  bashy google auth-import ~/Downloads/client_secret.json account=alice@example.com
  bashy google auth-status account=alice@example.com

## Runtime Environment Variables

- GWS_ACCOUNT: Required email address of the active Google account (or pass account=ADDR).
- GWS_CREDENTIALS_FILE: Explicit path to OAuth authorized_user JSON file (optional if imported via auth-import).
- GWS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_FILE: Explicit path to Service Account JSON key file.
- GWS_CONFIG_ROOT: Base directory for per-account credentials (default: ~/.config/bashy/google).
- GWS_BIN: Override path to the gws executable (default: gws on PATH).

Secrets (token, access_token, refresh_token, client_secret, private_key, password,
api_key, credentials, bearer, authorization) are strictly refused in argv (exit 2,
SECRET_VIA_ARGV).

## Single-Service Verbs

- Gmail: gmail-list, gmail-get, gmail-send, gmail-draft
- Calendar: calendar-list, calendar-get, calendar-create, calendar-update, calendar-delete, calendar-freebusy
- Tasks: tasklists-list, tasks-list, tasks-get, tasks-create, tasks-complete, tasks-update, tasks-delete
- Drive: drive-list, drive-search, drive-get, drive-upload, drive-mkdir
- Escape hatch: raw <service> <resource...>

## Composed Multi-Service Workflows

- mail-to-task <message-id> [tasklist=@default] [due=ISO] [notes=TEXT] [title=TEXT] [--dry-run]
- drive-share-mail <local-path> to=ADDR [subject=SUBJ] [body=TEXT] [parent=FOLDER_ID] [--dry-run]
- agenda [calendarId=primary] [tasklist=@default] [q=is:unread] [maxResults:=10]
~~~

set -euo pipefail
export BASHY_HINTS=off

if [[ "${1:-}" == "--help" || "${1:-}" == "-h" || "${1:-}" == "help" || "${1:-}" == "--skill" ]]; then
  inside=false
  while IFS= read -r line; do
    if [[ $line == '~~~skill as guide' ]]; then inside=true; continue; fi
    if [[ $inside == true && $line == '~~~' ]]; then break; fi
    if [[ $inside == true ]]; then printf '%s\n' "$line"; fi
  done < "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}"
  exit 0
fi

